From ec6243032736d85d4de1f048176db24696de59ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Snitzer <snitzer@kernel.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:34:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NFSD: Check only the thread's own flag in nfsd()'s loop

nfsd()'s loop called svc_thread_should_stop() before each svc_recv(),
reading the pool's sp_flags once a request.  On a busy pool another
CPU has written that line while the thread handled its request, so the
check missed, though svc_recv() checks the pool's flags itself after
its wait and marks the thread chosen to stop with RQ_VICTIM.  Check
that with svc_thread_chosen_to_stop().

Signed-off-by: Mike Snitzer <snitzer@kernel.org>
---
 fs/nfsd/nfssvc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/nfsd/nfssvc.c b/fs/nfsd/nfssvc.c
index 29ca36bb8832..450a1f3785ca 100644
--- a/fs/nfsd/nfssvc.c
+++ b/fs/nfsd/nfssvc.c
@@ -974,7 +974,7 @@ nfsd(void *vrqstp)
 	/*
 	 * The main request loop
 	 */
-	while (!svc_thread_should_stop(rqstp)) {
+	while (!svc_thread_chosen_to_stop(rqstp)) {
 		switch (svc_recv(rqstp, 5 * HZ)) {
 		case -ETIMEDOUT:
 			/* No work arrived within the timeout window */
-- 
2.52.0

